  - Autoencoder
  - Ridgelets
  - FFT (Fourier transform)
- Create processes for evaluating:
  - reproduction accuracy
  - computation time/complexity
  - noise rejection
  - off-axis target performance
- Set up test batches:
  - Different noise levels
  - Different asterisms and target locations
  - Standardised sets of kolmogorov screens (n=1000)


Null Hypotheses:
1) The tomographic reproduction accuracy is not impacted by the choice of basis function.
2) Choice of basis function has no impact on noise rejection performance for a tomographic algorithm.
3) An on-axis target has the same performance as an off-axis target for tomographic reproduction.
4) Changing the asterism has no impact on tomographic reproduction.

We are also looking at computational complexity, which means recording tomographic reproduction time for each test, and memory usage.

